      "extract": "Introduction Bring’s curve is the genus 4 Riemann surface with the automorphism group of maximal size, S5 [3, 9, 10, 19]. It may be expressed as the complete intersection in P4 given by x1 + x2 + x3 + x4 + x5 = 0, x2 1 + x2 2 + x2 3 + x2 4 + x2 5 = 0, x3 1 + x3 2 + x3 3 + x3 4 + x3 5 = 0. Here the permutations of the coordinates xi make manifest the S5 symmetry. The curve naturally arises in the study of the general",
